.el .ds Aq '
.TH batten-release 1  batten 
.SH NAME
batten\-release \- Answer whether a release is installable as it says it is, hash its assets, and backfill its tracking
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBbatten release\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Answer whether a release is installable as it says it is, hash its assets, and backfill its tracking
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
batten\-release\-install(1)
Decide whether install.sh, the release matrix and the binstall manifest agree on every asset name, and that no binary is committed
.TP
batten\-release\-sums(1)
Hash a published release\*(Aqs own assets into a checksum manifest, never the manifest itself
.TP
batten\-release\-verify(1)
Exit 0 only if a release carries every asset, its checksums match, and it is published and immutable at its own tag
.TP
batten\-release\-path(1)
Print whether a head may write main: its pin is inherited, or it changes only the release paths to a verified published release
.TP
batten\-release\-discard(1)
Delete a draft release and its tag; do nothing for no release; refuse a published one
.TP
batten\-release\-in\-flight(1)
Exit 0 when no release is in flight, 1 naming the one that is
.TP
batten\-release\-land\-state(1)
Print the land job\*(Aqs branch for a release: skip\-to\-f, resume\-at\-d, burned, draft\-ok, draft\-bad or absent
.TP
batten\-release\-bump\-unusable(1)
Move a burned or stray\-tagged version to the next one in all four release paths, as one commit on the release branch
.TP
batten\-release\-guard(1)
Exit 0 only when a build of the commit may upload into the release: a draft that targets it
.TP
batten\-release\-cut(1)
Discard any draft of the version, draft it at the release head and dispatch its build
.TP
batten\-release\-pin(1)
Print the release batten.toml pins, in the working tree or at a revision
.TP
batten\-release\-settings(1)
Exit 0 only when the rulesets and release settings the release path rests on hold
.TP
batten\-release\-backfill(1)
Dispatch a backfill workflow once per release tag, oldest first, waiting on each run and stopping at the first that does not succeed
.TP
batten\-release\-help(1)
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
